# DJ Demafidem (bouyonmusique.com, wave 26 parity, 2026-10-20)
# Sources used (all opened 2026-10-20):
# - Bandcamp, Soundway Records, Road Fever album page: compilation released May 9, 2025, compiled by Rozaly, mastering and vinyl cut The Carvery, vinyl pressing Garcia & Co, design Wolfe Hall Studio, photography Selwyn De Wind; vinyl Side A track 4 DJ Demafidem, On Di Road Riddim, 2:50; digital listing track 4 DJ Demafidem, On Di Road (2023), 2:50, and no other DJ Demafidem track in the 25 track digital listing; notes describe instrumental Dennery Segment and Bouyon riddims originally made for vocalists, minimal 150+ BPM, FL percussion packs, DJ and vox samples and synth riffs, bridging trap, drill, dancehall, sped up Haitian konpa and Angolan kuduro, and state in one sentence that Dominica increasingly influential Bouyon sound thrives through ScarnX and Guadeloupe-based Shazdown Mmw & DJ Demafidem; cassette is a 55 and a half minute mix by DJ Intl Prostyle with the full 26 track digital download, while the digital listing shown on the page counts 25 tracks.
# - Bandcamp Daily, Album of the Day review by Maria Barrios, May 12, 2025: London based Soundway Records, carnival riddims, Dennery segment and bouyon at 140 BPM or faster, laptop and Fruity Loops production; it names DJ Demafidem among the acts whose tracks power the compilation, alongside Ransum Records and the late G6 Productions, and it describes On Di Road and Bouyon Beam together, with punchy intros featuring synth stabs and vocal samples, as examples of the producers reimagining traditional music. The review hyperlinks the DJ Demafidem name to a SoundCloud page; that SoundCloud page could not be opened and verified in this session, so its address is not printed and it is not used as a sameAs entry.
# - Resident Advisor, Road Fever review by Cameron Cook, published May 21, 2025: 25 track list with DJ Demafidem, On Di Road at position 4; bouyon described as coming from Dominica and hovering at the 150 BPM mark, riddims usually voiced and here stripped down; the review gives no DJ Demafidem specific passage.
# - Patta, Road Fever feature (published May 12, 2025): compiled by Amsterdam based, Curacao raised Rozaly, mixed by DJ Intl Prostyle in Saint Lucia, 55 and a half minutes, BPM rarely dips below 150, DJ Demafidem listed among the contributing production crews, the compilation zeroes in on Dennery Segment from Saint Lucia and Bouyon from Dominica and Guadeloupe, out on vinyl, digital and limited cassette, with a short film by Rozaly and Selwyn De Wind.
# Aggregator note: Viberate and similar aggregator pages circulate other titles and a different base claim under the DJ Demafidem name. Aggregators were used for discovery only in this research; none of those titles was verified on a primary platform page opened in session, so none is printed as fact, none enters the structured data, and no aggregator address is used as a sameAs entry.
# Searches with no other result (2026-10-20): no standalone DJ Demafidem artist page, biography, interview, real name or solo release outside Road Fever was verified on Spotify, Apple Music, Shazam, Deezer, Qobuz, SoundCloud, Audiomack, YouTube or Discogs during this research. This profile prints none of those things and carries exactly one recording in its structured data.

